WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
Want to go now to

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.402
Democratic Congresswoman Ilhan Omar.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.170
She is joined by her guest for tonight's

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.238
State of the Union.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.073
Andre Lock Senior is.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:07.741
22 year old

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.943
son Amir was shot and killed last year

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.245
while police executed a no knock warrant

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.813
in Minneapolis.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.515
And Congresswoman Omar is introducing

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.983
legislation named after Amir

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.452
Lock to end the use of no knock warrants.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.554
I appreciate both of you being with me

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.355
very much.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.490
And Congresswoman,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.724
I'd like to begin with you

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.192
and the overall

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.360
framing of this speech

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.661
such that we understand it.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.697
You just heard Phil Mattingly's reporting

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.498
the President Biden

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:32.732
is going to make the case tonight

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.200
for bipartisanship.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.201
Some of his words

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.636
will include this phrase.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.370
There is no reason

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.272
we can't work to together

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.607
and that his vision for the country

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.641
is to unite it.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:41.975
Of course,

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.843
he's talking to a room with the Speaker

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.045
McCarthy behind him.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.346
Some of the Republicans in that room

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:46.980
are the very ones

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.281
who just kicked you off the House.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.749
Foreign Affairs Committee.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:50.917
Is he right to work

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.985
with those Republicans,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.820
including Speaker Kevin McCarthy?

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.390
So, you know, the president

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.558
has always been understood

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.192
as someone

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.995
who can unite a divided country.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.329
That's one of the reasons

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.665
people voted for him.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.434
You know, instead of voting for Trump,

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.701
I think it's really important

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.670
for there to be few people

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.671
that we identify

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.806
that we can work

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.841
with in a bipartisan manner.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.010
If you remember many

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.244
of the pieces of legislation

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.412
that we've moved

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.580
in, a slim majority

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.048
last in the last Congress,

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.484
a lot of them had bipartisanship

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.753
support, whether it was the bipartisan

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.923
gun bill, whether it was

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.058
the infrastructure legislation.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:32.692
There was just

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.127
there were a lot of moments

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.095
where we had that.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.164
And I think the president asking for that

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.966
moving forward.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.501
It's going to be really important

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.269
for anything to get done in the House.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.604
And of course, he is going to be talking

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.106
about police reform as well.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.173
And I want to get to that.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.675
But an email just came out

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:49.709
that I want to give you a chance

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:50.543
to respond to

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.445
because your Republican colleagues

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.246
are fundraising

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:53.980
off your removal

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.049
from the House Foreign Affairs Committee.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.350
The Republican Congressman, Brian

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.385
Mast of Florida just sent out an email

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.820
with the subject line,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.989
We just banned Ilhan Omar

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.190
and the email says

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.259
she is a rabid anti-Semite

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.660
whose position on the Foreign Affairs

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.362
Committee was a massive liability

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.731
for our country's national security.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.365
Congresswoman, he's

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.433
fundraising off of that.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.101
He's calling you a rabid anti-Semite.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.669
I wanted to give you a chance

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.637
to respond to that.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:19.806
Not only

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.275
is this a truly bigoted

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.045
act and speech,

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:29.249
it is really important for us to remember

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:32.085
just how partizan this vote was.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:32.285
You know,

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.419
many of my colleagues

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.622
talked about how this was an attack.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.422
I've talked about

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.526
how their bigoted actions were rooted

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:39.993
in the fact

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.595
that they didn't want a Muslim person,

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:45.064
someone who was an immigrant from Africa

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:49.269
and someone who was a refugee

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.237
being a voice on

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.039
on the Foreign Affairs Committee.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.074
This is a new McCarthyism.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.110
I think it's beneath them

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.012
to to be doing this,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.147
especially the speaker

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.549
denigrates his leadership

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.083
by raising money off

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.352
of committee assignments.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.754
But what can we expect?

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.123
This is the Republican Party

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:13.426
that is now run by conspiracy theorists.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.361
He went on folks

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.931
and folks who would rather run a circus

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.133
than a house.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.568
The president will also address

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.802
police reform.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:23.403
And Andre,

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.171
your son was killed by officers

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.340
executing a no knock warrant,

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.509
which was not related to your son.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:31.344
He was an illegal possession of a gun

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.046
Officer said they considered

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.214
that a threat.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.014
Prosecutors said

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:35.548
there wasn't

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.216
enough evidence

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.317
to justify charges

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.485
against any of those officers.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.187
Now, of course, you're there tonight.

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.121
With Congresswoman Omar

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.690
because she is putting forth

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.391
legislation named after your son,

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.394
which would end no knock warrants.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.663
When you look at Congress

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.832
and you look at the division there,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.867
do you have hope that this legislation

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:55.435
will pass?

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.003
I do.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:57.904
I have hope, and I

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.606
believe that it will pass.

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:01.975
And I actually I know that it's times

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.677
that if everything happens in seasons,

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:05.712
it is time for something

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:06.646
to happen at this point,

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:10.383
because no knock warrants are a high risk

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.353
so predominantly black and brown people.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.289
And we're continuing to lose our lives

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.791
for something that shouldn't be.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.361
So I truly believe that

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.896
by this bill being passed,

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.366
the mere fact that we know

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.834
that that it will save

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.068
not only civilian lives,

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:31.471
but also save police lives as well.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:32.672
And Andre,

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.573
what do you want to hear

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.541
from the president tonight?

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.211
Well, that is a

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:38.511
will for

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.481
our first officer honor to be here.

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.850
Congresswoman, thank you for inviting me

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.019
as a representation for my family,

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:48.755
the large family that was family

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.123
and also standing in the gaps

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:52.759
for Amir's mother,

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.895
Karen Wills, and the Morgan family.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:58.031
I hope to hear the president

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:01.234
stand strong on all reform

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.804
and I really don't know how to

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.506
I really don't know how to answer that

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:09.475
because, you know, it's

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.678
I expect a lot of things, you know, but

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:15.882
but mostly I'm hoping to see the no knock

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:20.053
bill possibly passed by Congress.

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:20.453
You know,

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.989
I was going to say

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:23.690
you know,

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.324
Andrea and I

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.958
were talking about this earlier.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.960
I think what we want to mostly hear

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.661
and what we've heard

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:31.030
from a lot of the families is they

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:34.033
they want to hear a speech

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.301
that's aspirational,

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.570
that's asking of Congress

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.273
to act around accountability reform,

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.142
one that will guarantee justice

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.611
and certainly make sure what

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.014
a new locked family has

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.982
experienced is never experienced

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.518
by other families across this country.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:54.887
But we also think that the president

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.657
still might have tools within his toolbox

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.892
when it comes to executive order.

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.260
So we're hoping to hear

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.964
what more can he do in regards to that.

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:06.332
But most of all,

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.701
we obviously also want to hear

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.170
holistically what the vision is for

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.805
for the country.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.475
And and we want it to be rooted

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.076
in justice. Yes.

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:18.411
Thank you both so very much.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.112
I appreciate it.

